/*--------------------------------*- C++ -*----------------------------------*\
| Mean age of air -- ventilation effectiveness, THE key chamber metric         |
| CLAUDE.md 8.4                                                                |
|                                                                              |
| Sanity target: the volume-mean age should land near the nominal residence     |
| time tau = V_air / Q.                                                         |
|                                                                              |
|     Q = 5 m3/h    tau = 1.82 s                                                |
|     Q = 2.5       tau = 3.6 s                                                 |
|     Q = 1.25      tau = 7.3 s                                                 |
|                                                                              |
| A mean well above tau means dead volume. Expect the hood (0.72 L, ~29 % of    |
| the chamber, sitting entirely above the jet) to be the worst region by a wide |
| margin -- this function object is how that gets demonstrated rather than      |
| asserted.                                                                     |
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

age
{
    type            age;
    libs            (fieldFunctionObjects);

    // Steady run: solve once at write time. It is a transport solve, not free.
    writeControl    writeTime;
    executeControl  writeTime;

    diffusion       on;      // include turbulent diffusion, not just advection
    tolerance       1e-6;
    nCorr           5;
    schemesField    age;
    log             true;
}

// Volume mean, so the number can be tracked and compared against tau directly.
ageMean
{
    type            volFieldValue;
    libs            (fieldFunctionObjects);
    writeControl    writeTime;
    log             true;
    writeFields     false;
    regionType      all;
    operation       volAverage;
    fields          (age);
}

ageMax
{
    $ageMean;
    operation       max;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// THE VERIFICATION. Do not report an age result without reading this number.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Sandberg's ventilation theory gives one EXACT identity: the flux-weighted
// mean age of the air LEAVING the domain equals the nominal time constant
//
//     <age>_exhaust  ==  tau  =  V_air / Q
//
// for ANY steady flow, whatever the internal recirculation looks like. It is a
// statement of mass conservation on the age field, not a modelling result, so
// it holds for a short-circuiting chamber exactly as it does for a well-mixed
// one. That makes it a free, sharp check on the age SOLVE:
//
//     ageOutlet ~ tau   ->  the transport equation converged
//     ageOutlet != tau  ->  it did not, and ageMean/ageMax are meaningless
//
// This matters here because the age equation is essentially pure advection
// (in a laminar case nu_eff is molecular, so there is almost no diffusion to
// conditionit) and it is genuinely hard to solve in a chamber with a stagnant
// hood and closed recirculation streamlines -- regions whose age is set by
// almost no boundary information at all.
//
// Measured 2026-08-15 at Q = 1.25 m3/h, m0: tau = 7.29 s.
//
// weightedAreaAverage + weightField phi is the FLUX weighting the identity
// requires. A plain areaAverage is NOT the same quantity and will not equal tau.
ageOutlet
{
    type            surfaceFieldValue;
    libs            (fieldFunctionObjects);
    writeControl    writeTime;
    log             true;
    writeFields     false;
    regionType      patch;
    name            outlet;
    operation       weightedAreaAverage;
    weightField     phi;
    fields          (age);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Where the dead volume actually is
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The volume mean alone says the chamber is badly ventilated; it does not say
// WHERE. These two zones are the ones the design question turns on:
//
//   hoodZone    everything above the box top (z > 96.667 mm) -- 0.72 L, ~29 % of
//               the chamber, sitting entirely ABOVE the jet with no direct
//               forced-convection path into it. CLAUDE.md 6.1 predicts this is
//               the worst-ventilated region by a wide margin; this is the number
//               that confirms or refutes that, rather than asserting it.
//               In Phase 2 it is also where the LED heat goes, so a high age
//               here and a warm cap are the same finding.
//
//   canopyZone  the growing volume itself, tray top to 50 mm. This is the one
//               that matters agronomically -- stale air over the crop is what
//               the whole study is about.
//
// Both zones are built by system/topoSetDict and exist in every case.
ageHood
{
    $ageMean;
    regionType      cellZone;
    name            hoodZone;
    operation       volAverage;
}

ageCanopy
{
    $ageMean;
    regionType      cellZone;
    name            canopyZone;
    operation       volAverage;
}

